83
00:05:30,633 --> 00:05:32,913
Now, back to the story.

84
00:05:32,953 --> 00:05:36,673
In April 2024, Zimbabwe tried again,

85
00:05:36,713 --> 00:05:41,473
with a new currency called ZiG,
short for Zimbabwe Gold.

86
00:05:41,513 --> 00:05:47,393
The central bank said ZiG was backed by
hard assets: gold and foreign currency.

87
00:05:47,433 --> 00:05:52,473
It started trading at about thirteen
and a half ZiG to one US dollar.

88
00:05:52,553 --> 00:05:55,886
Five months later, in September 2024,

89
00:05:55,940 --> 00:05:59,620
the central bank devalued it
by about forty-three percent,

90
00:05:59,646 --> 00:06:02,353
to around twenty-six ZiG per dollar.

91
00:06:02,393 --> 00:06:07,593
That means anyone holding ZiG suddenly had
money that bought far fewer dollars than

92
00:06:07,673 --> 00:06:12,073
the day before. And that is
exactly the kind of moment people

93
00:06:12,713 --> 00:06:18,353
remember. The plan was to make ZiG
Zimbabwe's only currency by 2030.

94
00:06:18,393 --> 00:06:23,073
But in January 2026,
the central bank changed course.

95
00:06:23,113 --> 00:06:28,073
Instead of a fixed date, it set
conditions first: low inflation,

96
00:06:28,153 --> 00:06:31,633
enough reserves to pay for
three to six months of imports,

97
00:06:31,673 --> 00:06:33,433
and a stable exchange rate.

98
00:06:33,513 --> 00:06:34,633
In other words,

99
00:06:34,713 --> 00:06:39,993
the US dollar goes only when people trust
the local currency enough to hold it.

100
00:06:40,872 --> 00:06:43,712
So where does that leave Zimbabwe today?

101
00:06:44,072 --> 00:06:47,432
According to the Confederation
of Zimbabwe Industries,

102
00:06:47,512 --> 00:06:52,152
seventy-seven percent of business sales
were in US dollars in the first half of

103
00:06:52,232 --> 00:06:57,312
2026, up from sixty-three and a
half percent two years earlier.

104
00:06:57,592 --> 00:06:59,192
And by another estimate,

105
00:06:59,272 --> 00:07:03,992
more than eighty percent of deposits
and transactions are in US dollars.

106
00:07:04,312 --> 00:07:09,992
The reason is trust. After
living through 2008 and 2019,

107
00:07:10,072 --> 00:07:14,472
many people would rather hold money that
their own central bank cannot print.

108
00:07:14,712 --> 00:07:19,992
A shop owner who sells in US dollars knows
that what she earns today will still buy

109
00:07:20,072 --> 00:07:22,352
roughly the same stock next month.

110
00:07:22,632 --> 00:07:25,672
And a lot of those
dollars come from outside.

111
00:07:25,712 --> 00:07:30,552
The Reserve Bank of Zimbabwe says diaspora
remittances brought in about two point

112
00:07:30,632 --> 00:07:34,472
four five billion US dollars in 2025.

113
00:07:34,592 --> 00:07:37,672
South Africa is home to
many of those senders.

114
00:07:37,752 --> 00:07:39,672
In the 2022 census,

115
00:07:39,872 --> 00:07:44,392
about one million people living in
South Africa were born in Zimbabwe,

116
00:07:44,472 --> 00:07:48,152
the largest group of people
born outside the country.

117
00:07:48,272 --> 00:07:53,192
So every month, money, airtime
and data cross the Limpopo,

118
00:07:53,272 --> 00:07:56,912
to parents, children and
grandparents back home.

119
00:07:57,352 --> 00:08:01,912
Let's recap. Zimbabwe's own
dollar collapsed in 2008,

120
00:08:01,992 --> 00:08:04,632
when prices doubled roughly every day,

121
00:08:04,712 --> 00:08:09,432
and a hundred trillion dollar note
was worth about thirty US dollars.

122
00:08:09,512 --> 00:08:14,365
In 2009, the country switched to
the US dollar and other currencies,

123
00:08:14,419 --> 00:08:16,952
and the runaway prices stopped.

124
00:08:17,032 --> 00:08:19,712
Every attempt to bring
back a local currency,

125
00:08:19,752 --> 00:08:23,192
from bond notes to the RTGS dollar to ZiG,

126
00:08:23,312 --> 00:08:25,912
has had to win back people's trust.

127
00:08:25,992 --> 00:08:30,952
And today, most business sales in
Zimbabwe still happen in US dollars,

128
00:08:31,032 --> 00:08:34,392
with billions coming
in from family abroad.

